// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, defense-evasion, T1098, T1484.001
// Description: Detects execution of bloodyAD, an Active Directory privilege escalation framework that supports
//   DACL manipulation, password resets, group membership changes, RBCD configuration, UAC flag
//   modification, and computer account creation.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/CravateRouge/bloodyAD
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6b9ade7935a13d35a57e75ff2587fbedcc53ef56/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_hktl_bloodyad.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "/bloodyAD" or ((FolderPath contains "/python" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName contains "python") and ProcessCommandLine contains "bloodyAD")
